Third-party components
----------------------

fints2camt uses, but does not contain or modify, the following libraries. They are
installed as separate Python packages (pinned in pyproject.toml) and remain under their
own licenses:

* python-fints (package "fints") — GNU Lesser General Public License v3 or later
  (LGPL-3.0-or-later), https://github.com/raphaelm/python-fints
  fints2camt links to it as an unmodified, separately installed library; you may replace
  it with a modified version of your own (e.g. `pip install` another build into the
  environment or the container image), as the LGPL allows. Its dependency "enum-tools"
  is LGPL-3.0-or-later as well.
* lxml — BSD-3-Clause, https://lxml.de
* httpx — BSD-3-Clause, https://www.python-httpx.org

Their transitive dependencies (among others mt-940, sepaxml, requests, certifi, bleach,
text-unidecode) carry their own licenses, listed in each package's metadata
(`pip show --verbose <package>`). The container image additionally contains the Debian
and Python base image (python:3.12-slim) with its own licenses.

The camt.053.001.02 XML schema in src/fints2camt/schemas/ is the ISO 20022 message
definition published by ISO 20022 / SWIFT, included unmodified for validation.
